 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "When `TESSEL_RUN_FROM_CLI` is `\"true\"`, `Tessel.run` does nothing and returns early. The check is at `src/tessel/app.py:695-705`.\n\n- If it isn't running inside the reloader, it first prints a red warning: \"Ignoring a call to 'app.run()' that would block the current 'tessel' CLI command. Only call 'app.run()' in an 'if __name__ == \"__main__\"' guard.\"\n- Inside the reloader it returns silently.\n- The dotenv loading and server startup below it are skipped, so calling `app.run()` at import time can't start a second server.\n\nThe variable is set by `TesselGroup.make_context` in `src/tessel/cli.py:667`, so any `tessel` CLI invocation turns `app.run()` into a no-op.",
